    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d20">

                <pb facs="0111" n="23" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg23"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Jusserand to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >French Embassy</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-02-13"><hi rendition="#italic">February 13,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>:</p>
                <p>My Government has just communicated to me that the Russian and Japanese
                    Governments having officially advised it of the state of war existing between
                    them it had decided to conform, in order to observe neutrality, to the
                    principles set down by the circular published in the <pb facs="0112" n="24"
                        xml:id="pg24"/> official journal of the Republic on April 27, 1898.<anchor
                        n="a" xml:id="d20-f1"/> I consider it my duty to bring these intentions to
                    the knowledge of your excellency and to mention that the above-named circular
                    has been communicated by my predecessor to the Department of State on the 11th
                    of May, 1898.</p>
                <p>Please accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jusserand.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
